        <span class="eyebrow">METHODS &amp; VALIDATION · JABODETABEK AIR-QUALITY NOWCAST</span>
        <h1>Can Jakarta forecast air it can no longer measure?</h1>
        <p class="standfirst">A stress test of a 24–72 hour PM2.5 nowcast for Greater Jakarta,
        {A.vintage.ground_first}–{A.vintage.ground_last}. The headline skill number survives its own
        baseline and fails a better one; the held-out panel shrinks from six sensors to one across the
        window it is measured on; and the last two instruments in the city disagreed by a factor of six
        before one of them went dark. The sparsity the case reports as context turns out to be the
        result.</p>
        <div class="byline">
          <span>openstudy.id</span>
          <span>{n0(A.panel.n_test_rows)} held-out station-hours</span>
          <span>{A.network.n_stations_total} registrations · {A.addresses.n_ever_reported} instruments</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <details class="glossary" id="glossary">
        <summary>
          <span>Plain-language glossary</span>
          <span class="gcount">{__glossary.length} terms this article uses</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="glossary-lede">
          Written for someone who knows the subject and not this vocabulary. The instrument
          and measurement terms come first, because those are the ones a specialist in the
          subject has no reason to know; the statistics follow.
        </p>
        <dl>
          {__glossary.map((g) => (
            <div>
